12
00:43:18,260 --> 00:43:24,260
Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer is a fictional reindeer created by Robert L.

13
00:46:54,782 --> 00:47:00,782
Rudolph is usually depicted as the ninth and youngest of Santa Claus's reindeer, using his
luminous red nose to lead the reindeer team and guide Santa's sleigh on Christmas Eve.

14
00:50:31,304 --> 00:50:37,304
Though he initially receives ridicule for his nose as a fawn, the brightness of his nose is
so powerful that it illuminates the team's path through harsh winter weather.

15
00:54:07,826 --> 00:54:13,826
Lankford, Jr., described Rudolph's story as "the fantasy story made to order for American children: each child
has the need to express and receive approval for their individuality and special qualities.

16
00:57:44,347 --> 00:57:50,347
Rudolph's story embodies the American Dream for the child, writ large because of the cultural significance of
Christmas."
Rudolph first appeared in a 1939 booklet written by May and published by Montgomery Ward, the department store.

17
01:01:20,869 --> 01:01:26,869
The story is owned by The Rudolph Company, LP and has been adapted into numerous forms including the song by Johnny Marks, the television special Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer, Rudolph's Shiny New Year, and Rudolph and
Frosty's Christmas in July from Rankin/Bass Productions, as well as Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer: The Movie and Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer and the Island of Misfit Toys from GoodTimes Entertainment.

18
01:04:57,391 --> 01:05:03,391
Character Arts, LLC manages the licensing for the
Rudolph Company, LP and DreamWorks Classics.

19
01:08:33,913 --> 01:08:39,913
In many countries, Rudolph has become a figure of Christmas folklore.

20
01:12:10,434 --> 01:12:16,434
2014 marked the 75th anniversary of the character and the 50th
anniversary of the Rankin/Bass television special.

21
01:15:46,956 --> 01:15:52,956
A series of postage stamps featuring Rudolph was issued by the
United States Postal Service on November 6, 2014.

22
01:19:23,478 --> 01:19:29,478
The film explores themes of snow, christmas spirit, christmas.
